{
  "name": "priority_scheduling",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "critical_ask",
      "op": "ASK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Design a REST API for a simple TODO list application. What are the core endpoints? Provide 3-4 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "name": "critical_think",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "{0}\n\nBased on this API design, what are the key data models needed? Describe the schema in 3-4 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "name": "critical_reason",
      "op": "REASON",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "{0}\n\nGiven these data models, what are the main scalability challenges? Propose a solution in 3-4 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "critical_final",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "{0}\n\nSummarize the complete design (API + data model + scalability) in 4-5 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "name": "bg_naming_analysis",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Analyze common REST API naming conventions for TODO applications. What are the best practices? Provide 4-5 examples."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "name": "bg_auth_research",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Research authentication patterns for TODO applications. Compare JWT vs session-based auth. Which is better and why? Provide 4-5 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "bg_database_analysis",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Compare PostgreSQL vs MongoDB for a TODO list application. What are the tradeoffs? Which would you choose and why? Provide 4-5 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "name": "bg_caching_research",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Research caching strategies for TODO list APIs. Where should caching be applied? What are the tradeoffs? Provide 4-5 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "name": "bg_monitoring_analysis",
      "op": "THINK",
      "attributes": {
        "template_str": "Analyze monitoring approaches for TODO list applications. What metrics should be tracked? What tools are commonly used? Provide 4-5 sentences."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "name": "bg_report",
      "op": "MERGE",
      "attributes": {}
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "name": "print",
      "op": "PRINT",
      "attributes": {
        "message": "=== USER-VISIBLE OUTPUT (Critical Path) ===\n\n{0}\n\nThis is the CRITICAL PATH result that the user sees.\nWith priority scheduling, this should complete FIRST,\neven if background tasks are still running."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "name": "print_1",
      "op": "PRINT",
      "attributes": {
        "message": "=== BACKGROUND ANALYTICS (Low Priority) ===\n\nNaming conventions: {0}\n\nAuthentication: {1}\n\nDatabase choice: {2}\n\nCaching strategy: {3}\n\nMonitoring: {4}\n\nThis background work completed after the critical path."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "name": "all_done",
      "op": "WAIT_ALL",
      "attributes": {}
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "name": "print_2",
      "op": "PRINT",
      "attributes": {
        "message": "=== PRIORITY SCHEDULING STRESS TEST ===\n\nCritical path (ask\u2192think\u2192reason\u2192final): COMPLETED\nBackground tasks (5 parallel speculative nodes): COMPLETED\n\nO0: All 9 nodes scheduled with equal priority (random order)\nO2: Critical path prioritized \u2192 faster user-visible response\n\nMetric: Critical path completion time should be LOWER in O2 under contention."
      }
    },
